{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Cast.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Push"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_add_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_add_eq","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L116-L123","doc":"A `d`-fold generalisation: for `Z = N + d` the split scales *linearly* in the\ncharge asymmetry `d` and in nothing else. So even off the `d = 1` ladder the\nbound offers only one free integer, and it is not `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_eq_zero_of_flux_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_eq_zero_of_flux_eq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L108-L114","doc":"The split vanishes identically when the two fluxes agree. So a charge-blind\nflux assignment predicts **no** mirror splitting at all — the bound cannot even\nproduce the effect, let alone its `A`-dependence. This is the degenerate case\nthat forces `φp ≠ φn` before any fitting begins. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_succ_eq_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_succ_eq_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L100-L106","doc":"Stated as the falsifiable claim: **two different nuclei on the `d = 1` ladder\nhave equal splits.** The AME ladder disagrees by a factor of 13.63 across\n`A = 3…63`, so the hypotheses of this theorem — a vertex-transitive carrier, a\nflux depending only on charge, and a saturated bound — cannot all hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_succ_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_succ_const","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L91-L98","doc":"**The refutation, for the `d = 1` ladder.** Every mirror pair with\n`Z = N + 1` — which is the whole `A = 2Z − 1` series the arc scores against —\ngets the *same* split `C·a·m·(φp − φn)`, with no dependence on `N` whatsoever. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit_eq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**The split factorises**: all dependence on the nucleus enters through the\nsingle integer `Z − N`, multiplying the flux *difference*.\n\nThis is the charge-blindness of eq. (43) made explicit: the topology (`a`), the\nconstant (`C`) and the minimum (`m`) survive the subtraction untouched, and the\ncomponent counts survive only in the combination `Z − N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.mirrorSplit","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L72-L77","doc":"The mirror split: the bound's value on `(Z, N)` minus its value on the\nmirror partner `(N, Z)`. Mirror partners share `A = Z + N`, share the carrier\nlink, and share `m` — the swap only relabels which components are charged, so\nevery ingredient except the charge assignment is held fixed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.fhBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.fhBound","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/FreedmanHeMirrorSplitChargeBlind.lean#L62-L70","doc":"The right-hand side of the Freedman–He link bound (Komendarczyk eq. (43))\nspecialised to a **vertex-transitive** carrier and a **charge-only** flux.\n\n`C` is the pure constant `(π/16)^{1/4}`, `a` the common component value\n`ac(L_k, L)`, `m` the factor `min_k |Flux(X_k)|`, and the `Z` proton components\ncarry flux `φp` while the `N` neutron components carry `φn`. The sum\n`Σ_k ac(L_k,L)|Flux(X_k)|` collapses to `a · (Z·φp + N·φn)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}